course: dictionary
lesson: 14357
title: Oncoming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Oncoming» is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you that something is coming towards you or moving nearer. «Look out for oncoming traffic» means watch for cars and bikes that are driving towards you.
explain: Use the words around it as clues. «The cyclist moved over to avoid an oncoming car.» The car is coming towards the cyclist, so oncoming must mean moving nearer. Check by swapping in your meaning: "to avoid a car coming towards them" still makes sense.
explain: Writers use oncoming to build tension. «The oncoming storm» tells you the storm is getting closer and something is about to happen. You can feel the danger in the word before the storm even arrives.
fact: Oncoming means coming towards you or moving nearer.
fact: «Oncoming traffic» means vehicles that are driving towards you.
fact: «Oncoming storm» means a storm that is getting closer.
fact: Oncoming is a road-safety word: before you cross, look out for oncoming traffic.
fact: Oncoming is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as traffic, storm or army.
exercise: «Look out for oncoming traffic before you cross the road.» What does oncoming mean? | Parked at the side of the road | Going away from you | *Coming towards you | Standing still
exercise: «The oncoming army marched over the hill.» What is moving nearer? | A picnic in the park | A bird flying away | A quiet lake | *An army
exercise: Find and copy the word that means moving nearer: «The oncoming bus flashed its lights.» | bus | *oncoming | flashed | lights
test: «On a narrow road, the cyclist moved over to let the oncoming car pass.» Why did the cyclist move over? | To race a car going the same way | To wave at a friend | *To let a car coming towards them pass | To stop for a rest
test: «The walkers heard the oncoming train before they saw it.» What is oncoming here? | *The train, moving nearer to them | The path under their feet | The walkers, moving away | The sky
exam: Ruby says oncoming means going away from you. Is she right? | Yes, it means going away | No, it means very quiet | Yes, it means standing still | *No, it means coming towards you
